  "body": "Closes #1173\nClaim: cloud/fb-quickwins-sonnet\nAuthor model: Sonnet 5.5 (cloud/fb-quickwins-sonnet)\nReviewer model: Opus 5.5 (cloud/review-1226-opus, round 1: REQUEST CHANGES, fixed in the head; round 2 pending)\n\n### Problem\nThe app-lock switch read « Verrouiller l’app (Face ID / code) » on every device, promising Face ID on Touch ID iPads and passcode-only devices (HIG › Managing accounts: refer only to authentication methods available in the current context; also an App Review risk). The lock is new in SwiftHFR (LOT-173, GAP-168/169): no legacy counterpart.\n\n### Cause\n`SecuritySettingsSections` used a fixed string; nothing read `LAContext.biometryType`.\n\n### Change\n- `AppLockMethod` (`faceID`, `touchID`, `opticID`, `codeOnly`), built from `LABiometryType` (`init(biometry:)`), with `switchTitle`: « Verrouiller l’app (Face ID / code) », « … (Touch ID / code) », « … (Optic ID / code) », « Verrouiller l’app (code) » when the device reports no biometry.\n- `DeviceOwnerAuthenticating.method` (the existing seam of the lock): `LocalAuthenticationAuthenticator` reads `biometryType` after `canEvaluatePolicy(.deviceOwnerAuthenticationWithBiometrics)` (which is what fills it, **whatever that call returns**: a Face ID iPhone with no face enrolled, or locked out, still reports `.faceID` and still shows « Face ID / code », which is right: the device offers that method; review round 1 corrected my first comment and Mac check on this point). Previews and the test double return `.faceID`.\n- `AppLockModel.switchTitle` forwards it; `SecuritySettingsSections` uses it. The authentication policy itself (`deviceOwnerAuthentication`, biometrics then code) is unchanged.\n- `docs/lots/LOT-173-keychain-sync-lock.md` no longer quotes the fixed title (review round 1).\n\n### Tests\n`AppLockMethodTests` (written first): the title for each `LABiometryType` (`faceID`, `touchID`, `opticID`, `none`); the model takes its title from the authenticator for each method; the code-only title mentions no biometry. The real `LAContext` read is one line over a system API: Mac check on #893 (Touch ID iPad simulator shows « Touch ID »; a Face ID device shows « Face ID » even with no face enrolled; « code » only on a device that reports no biometry, e.g. an iPad without Touch ID). Not run here (Linux); `compile-check` runs on the head.\n\n---\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.ai/code)\n\nhttps://claude.ai/code/session_014QH2CDvQG8jqNrseTphdnF",
