   "body": "**Adversarial review (Opus 5.5, cloud/review-1226-opus, round 1): REQUEST CHANGES** — head 5d7faa69\n\n1. **Medium**: the comment at `App/SwiftHFR/AppLock/AppLockModel.swift:46` (`codeOnly`: \"No biometry (none, or none enrolled)\") is wrong, and so is the PR body's Mac check (\"a device without enrolled biometry shows « code »\"). Apple documents `LAContext.biometryType` as \"set only after you call `canEvaluatePolicy(_:error:)`, and is set no matter what the call returns\". If the device has the sensor but nothing is enrolled (or biometry is locked out), `canEvaluatePolicy(.deviceOwnerAuthenticationWithBiometrics)` returns false with `.biometryNotEnrolled` (or `.biometryLockout`), but `biometryType` still says `.faceID` or `.touchID`.\n   - Failing scenario: a Face ID iPhone with no face enrolled shows « Verrouiller l'app (Face ID / code) ». The Mac check on #893 will fail against what the PR says it checks.\n   - Fix, two options:\n     - (a) Keep the behaviour, which is HIG-compliant because the device does offer Face ID. Correct the comment, the PR body and the check.\n     - (b) If « code » is wanted when nothing is enrolled: when `canEvaluatePolicy` returns false with `.biometryNotEnrolled`, map to `.codeOnly`. Add a pure mapping `init(biometry:canUseBiometrics:)` with a test for each case.\n2. **Low**: `docs/lots/LOT-173-keychain-sync-lock.md:102` still quotes the fixed title \"Verrouiller l'app (Face ID / code)\" as the switch's text. The spec now contradicts the code (L08/L09). Update it in this PR to say the title depends on the device's biometry (#1173). GAP-169's \"Face ID / code lock\" is a feature summary, so no `### Ledger` edit is needed.\n3. **Detail**: `AppLockModel.switchTitle` → `LocalAuthenticationAuthenticator.method` creates a fresh `LAContext` and runs `canEvaluatePolicy` on every `body` evaluation of `SecuritySettingsSections`. That section also re-renders on account-sync changes. `canEvaluatePolicy` never shows UI and costs little, so this is acceptable. It also picks up an enrolment change on the next render. Computing it once per appearance is optional.\n4. **Detail**: the PR says the Mac check goes \"on #893\". I found no line for #1173 or #1226 there yet; only the morning summary names #1173 as assigned. Keep this as the author's to-do, with the expectation corrected per finding 1.\n\nNo other problems found:\n- **Concurrency**: the conformers are a stateless struct, a final class with `let method` and a private struct. The `LAContext` is local and not shared. A `@MainActor` model calling a sync, nonisolated getter is fine.\n- **`LABiometryType` API use**: `.opticID` (iOS 17+) and `.none` (not the deprecated `.typeNone`) are correct. `default` covers future cases.\n- **Tests**: they fail without the change (`.touchID` and `.codeOnly` rows).\n- **Other text**: `NSFaceIDUsageDescription` and the lock-cover text name no method.\n\n**Vérifié**\n- Read the diff 5d7faa69 against dev-swift.\n- Grepped every `DeviceOwnerAuthenticating` conformer (3 + preview) and every \"Face ID\" / `biometr` occurrence in App and docs.\n- SwiftLint on the changed files in a throwaway worktree: clean; worktree removed.\n- Read issue #1173, the PR body, the LOT-173 spec and #893 comments.\n- App tests not run (Linux).\n\n---\n_Generated by [Claude Code](https://claude.ai/code)_",
