   "body": "**Adversarial review (Opus 5.5, cloud/review-1226-opus-r2, round 2): APPROVE** — head f6f8c3fe\n\nBoth round-1 findings are fixed. `AppLockModel.swift:46-47` now says that a sensor with nothing enrolled, or one that is locked out, still reports `.faceID` or `.touchID`. The PR body says the same, and so does the Mac check line (\"a Face ID device shows « Face ID » even with no face enrolled\"). `git grep -n -i enrolled -- App docs` finds only the corrected comment, so no doc still says that a device with nothing enrolled shows « code ». In `LOT-173-keychain-sync-lock.md:102`, the strings \"Face ID\", \"Touch ID\", \"Optic ID\" and \"Verrouiller l'app (code)\" match `AppLockMethod.switchTitle`. The spec writes a straight apostrophe where the code has `’`, but that was already there before this PR.\n\nRemaining details (none blocks the merge):\n1. Detail, PR body, Tests section: the Mac check gives \"an iPad without Touch ID\" as the device that shows « code ». Every device that can run iOS 27 has Touch ID or Face ID, so a real device cannot show that case, and the hand check cannot test it. Fix: say that `.codeOnly` is covered by the unit test only. Optionally, check it on a simulator model that reports no biometry, if one exists.\n2. Detail, PR body, Change section: \"no longer quotes the fixed title\" goes a little too far. The spec still opens with the Face ID title, then says the method part changes with the device. That reads correctly; only the wording of the body needs adjusting.\n3. Detail, `AppLockModel.swift:107`: `switchTitle` creates a new `LAContext` and calls `canEvaluatePolicy` every time the settings section redraws. The cost is negligible today, but caching the value when the model is created would avoid it.\n\nFresh pass:\n- There are 4 `DeviceOwnerAuthenticating` conformers: the real one, `NoAuthentication`, `ScriptedAuthenticator` and `MethodAuthenticator`. All four implement `method`.\n- `method` is synchronous, nonisolated and `Sendable`, and is read from the `@MainActor` model, so there is no isolation problem.\n- The tests do not pass trivially. A model that hard-coded `.faceID` would fail the Touch ID, Optic ID and code cases, and a wrong mapping in `init(biometry:)` would fail the table test.\n- The authentication policy (`deviceOwnerAuthentication`) is unchanged.\n\n**Vérifié**\n- Delta `5d7faa69..f6f8c3fe` and the full diff `origin/dev-swift...f6f8c3fe`.\n- The live PR body at head f6f8c3fe.\n- `git grep` for `enrolled`, `Face ID / code` and the `DeviceOwnerAuthenticating` conformers.\n- SwiftLint on the changed files in a throwaway worktree: clean, worktree removed afterwards.\n- Not run: the app tests (Linux). The Compile check on f6f8c3fe is reported green by the caller; I did not check it myself.\n\n---\n_Generated by [Claude Code](https://claude.ai/code)_",
